    "body": "`not lock` should be removed since another worker might have already completed the job and deleted the lock. When I was trying to fix this locally, I realized that a bunch of unit tests broke when enforcing that a lock exists in this script. I fixed this by having `Job.prototype.moveToDelayed` take an `ignoreLock` parameter that passed in `0` as the token to the script, and checked it inside the script using:\r\n\r\n```\r\n  if ARGV[4] ~= \"0\" then\r\n    local lockKey = KEYS[3] .. ':lock'\r\n    if redis.call(\"GET\", lockKey) ~= ARGV[4] then\r\n      return -2\r\n    end\r\n  end\r\n```\r\n\r\n(this is how it's done in moveToFinished). That way the unit tests could use the special moveToDelayed() function that can ignore the lock.",
